counterexample:
Selective error erasure when the caller strictly lacks any programmatic way or reason to handle errors differently:
```rust
fn is_system_healthy() -> bool {
    check_db().is_ok() && check_cache().is_ok()
}
```

fix:
Define a composite error enum representing all potential pipeline errors, using `map_err` to adapt specific subsystem errors into clear variants.
```rust
enum PaymentError {
    Validation(ValidationError),
    Network(reqwest::Error),
}

fn process_payment(order_id: u64) -> Result<(), PaymentError> {
    validate_order(order_id).map_err(PaymentError::Validation)?;
    charge_card(order_id).map_err(PaymentError::Network)?;
    Ok(())
}
```
